#== News

== About me
I am a forth-year PhD student in the [https://https://math.ucsd.edu/ Department of Mathematics] at UC San Diego. I am very fortunate to be advised by 
[https://math.ucsd.edu/people/profiles/ioana-dumitriu Ioana Dumitriu] and [https://mathweb.ucsd.edu/~tkemp/ Todd Kemp]. 
Prior to UCSD, I received my M.Sc. degree in Mathematics from Texas A&M University, supervised by [https://www.math.tamu.edu/~manshel/ Michael Anshelevich], and B.Sc. degree in Mathematics from [https://ev.buaa.edu.cn/ Beihang University].

#== Education 

== Research Interests
My current research focuses on developing a theoretical understanding 
of fundamental algorithms in deep learning, using tools from high-dimensional probability. \n
- Random Matrix Theory and Free Probability Theory
- Deep Learning Theory 
- High-dimensional Statistics

